f348fc480be6ba64263f047f54","position":"1789048985244869001-cb694308-a51c-4ac4-91b7-7cbe45daa78b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Remediation update after change 2962 merged: manual Windows run 34466319475 showed the original fcntl collection failure was gone and the named Windows exclusive-leg proof step passed, but the continue-on-error Windows default suite exposed a follow-on topology-copy setup failure in tests/_topology_template.py. Local root cause: helpers used git -C against copied bare remotes, which fails under safe.bareRepository=explicit and can skip sibling remote rewrites; Windows paths may also be slash-normalized in Git config. Expanded file impact accordingly. Targeted validation now passes: 33 passed, 2 skipped for the fcntl guard modules plus tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated. Full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 lint/typecheck passed and pytest progressed past 50%, but I stopped it after ~82 minutes to avoid missing the cutoff; the observed active tests pass individually.","timestamp":1789046801369608001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Follow-up remediation pushed to Gerrit as change 2970 (Fix topology copy paths). This is the one honest remediation round for the Windows/manual-sweep follow-on failure exposed after change 2962 merged. Awaiting LLM-Review and Verified; if either fails past cutoff I will park as WIP with the next-step context.","timestamp":1789047045906551001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"07:00 cutoff parking context: change 2962 already merged and fixed the original Windows collection failure (manual run 34466319475: no fcntl ModuleNotFoundError; named Windows exclusive-leg proof step passed). That run exposed a follow-on topology-copy setup failure, so I made the allowed single remediation round in tests/_topology_template.py and pushed Gerrit change 2970 (WIP at cutoff). Evidence: targeted local validation passed with 33 passed, 2 skipped; pre-commit lint/typecheck passed; local make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 passed lint/typecheck and progressed past 50 percent before I stopped it for cutoff, with the two active tests passing individually. Gerrit change 2970 currently has LLM-Review +1 and no unresolved comments; Verified is still pending on GitHub run 34483084465, with ubuntu-latest py3.13 still in progress at 07:01. Next step for the next closer: if run 34483084465 reaches Verified +1, mark change 2970 ready, submit, fast-forward a fresh worktree to the merged SHA, rerun/observe Windows sweep evidence, then close this ticket; if CI fails, inspect that run and remediate from change 2970.","timestamp":1789048892542984001}],"created_at":1788996161663874001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"51314f12-fa38-4cd6-8440-fe58bbf3af63","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2ea6-af6e-c23b-4dc5"},{"link_uuid":"914b3f8a-4925-4d53-9c2e-8c85534b05f9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3389-7f25-66d0-4776"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe scheduled main `test.yml` `sweep (windows)` job failed on three consecutive scheduled runs (34321330218, 34353500045, 34391071987; 2026-09-08..09). The failure signature is a collection-time `ModuleNotFoundError` from `tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py`, followed by setup-error cascades in store/MCP round-trip tests. Ubuntu gating and macOS sweep pass on the same SHAs, so this is Windows-specific.\n\n## Suspected root cause\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py` imports the POSIX-only `fcntl` module at module import time. Windows has no `fcntl`, so pytest fails during collection before test-level setup or skip logic can run. The production lock abstraction already supports both POSIX and Windows (`src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py`); the red sweep appears to be a test portability bug in a POSIX-specific regression test for reclaiming a stale mkdir owner stamp after acquiring the fcntl leg.\n\n## Plan\n1. Confirm the Windows log points at `import fcntl` in `tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py` and inspect the production lock abstraction for the existing portable/Windows path.\n2. Add a module-level `pytest.mark.skipif(sys.platform == \"win32\", ...)` for this POSIX-only test module and guard the `fcntl` import so Windows collection skips cleanly instead of failing at import time. The skip reason must point at `tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py` for the native Windows lock-leg coverage.\n3. Keep the fix scoped to test portability; do not change production locking semantics unless investigation proves the production abstraction is faulty.\n4. Validate with the smallest local tests that can cover the changed module and the existing import/lock guard tests, then run the repo verification command. Trigger a Windows `test.yml` sweep via `workflow_dispatch` for the submitted patchset or merged ref (or use the next scheduled sweep if dispatch is unavailable) and record the run id/result as the Windows proof.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The root cause is identified from the Windows CI log and recorded in the ticket: collection fails because the POSIX-only `fcntl` import is evaluated on Windows before any guard can skip the module.\n- [ ] `tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py` has a module-level Windows skip plus guarded `fcntl` import, so Windows collection skips the POSIX-only fcntl regression test instead of raising `ModuleNotFoundError`; the skip reason cites `tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py` as the native Windows lock-leg coverage.\n- [ ] No production lock behavior is weakened for POSIX or Windows.\n- [ ] Local targeted validation passes for `tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py`, `tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py`, `tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py`, and `tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py` on this host.\n- [ ] `env -u GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL -u GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM -u GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes before push, or any local baseline/environment failure is classified and Gerrit `Verified +1` supplies the gating verdict.\n- [ ] Gerrit CI reports `Verified +1`; a Windows `test.yml` sweep is triggered by `workflow_dispatch` for this patchset/merged ref or observed from the next scheduled run, and its run id/result are recorded before closing.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py` from the fresh worktree.\n- `env -u GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL -u GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM -u GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` before push.\n- Gerrit CI `Verified +1` before submit.\n- Windows `test.yml` sweep/manual workflow evidence is recorded with run id and conclusion before close.\n\n## File impact\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py` — collection-time guard for a POSIX-only fcntl regression test.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py","reason":"guard POSIX-only fcntl regression test so Windows sweep collects"},{"path":"tests/_topology_template.py","reason":"copy-isolation remediation for Windows/manual sweep setup cascade and local safe.bareRepository=explicit baseline failure"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2ea6-af6e-c23b-4dc5"],["relates_to","3389-7f25-66d0-4776"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f2a51a23-636c-4343-8eaa-643cc7f536bb","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","windows"],"ticket_id":"15c8-0940-df83-46b1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"sweep (windows) red 3 consecutive scheduled runs: POSIX-only import/setup in store/MCP write-lock tests","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1b502b0b-927a-4ff9-b894-671af4afd919","8fd2f9e7-ffdb-494f-9f5e-22c590f8f7d0","8ecde162-f01f-477f-8497-13bca38ed231","c0ac8709-e138-4e17-b942-8bf964697fb1","af2a35a8-8e70-4a2e-8174-343fcfbd7b57","9e2644fc-38b0-4218-a6d2-f76f64173a62","51314f12-fa38-4cd6-8440-fe58bbf3af63","da3f62e2-47c7-4b3e-a68c-2b511ea36c8c","a72dc250-6724-43a9-8567-37ba1e43f6d5","511c6731-4955-431d-a32a-1d442438d041","914b3f8a-4925-4d53-9c2e-8c85534b05f9","5a906e4f-855f-4f4e-bc6b-b019c1006651","f2a51a23-636c-4343-8eaa-643cc7f536bb","cb694308-a51c-4ac4-91b7-7cbe45daa78b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789062126330007001,"uuid":"dafd915e-1814-4beb-b596-d90baab64028"}